abstract: >-
  CSI (CRISM Spectral Interrogator) is an IDL-based graphical tool for
  visualization, spectral analysis, interpretation, and documentation of
  Compact Reconnaissance Imaging Spectrometer for Mars (CRISM) data. CSI
  supports region-of-interest definition, spectral extraction and ratioing,
  comparison with MICA and laboratory reference spectra, and export of
  interpreted locations for use in external mapping and GIS applications.
